# Training inputs and intermediates. The corpora are large and re-downloadable;
# only wake/models/ ships. See README.md for the pipeline, data/README.md for
# what lives in data/.
#
# data/* rather than data/ so the negations below work: git does not descend
# into an ignored directory, so a negation under `data/` would never match.
data/*
!data/README.md

# Recordings are committed. A few MB each, and unlike the corpora they cannot
# be regenerated — my_voice/ is the highest-value input the pipeline has, and
# ab_jarvis/ is the control set for comparing against openWakeWord's pretrained
# model on the same voice, mic and room.
!data/my_voice/
!data/ab_jarvis/

output/
logs/
__pycache__/
